  "goodToKnow": "Der Apostel is an apostle, one of the twelve disciples sent out by Jesus. Die Apostelgeschichte is the Acts of the Apostles. Figuratively, it means a zealous advocate, often ironic: ein Apostel der Sparsamkeit (a preacher of thrift). Saint Boniface is called der Apostel der Deutschen for converting Germanic tribes in the 8th century. From Greek apostolos (messenger). Plural unchanged: die Apostel."
